# Production dependency RANGES for the deployed web service: the source of the
# hashed lock in backend/requirements.txt, which Railway and CI install. Edit
# this file, then regenerate the lock from backend/:
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt
#
# The engine's runtime dependencies are listed here as well as in
# pyproject.toml. pyproject.toml holds the ranges the published package
# promises its users; this file holds what the deployed service runs. The
# engine itself is installed with `pip install --no-deps .` after the lock, and
# CI runs `pip check` so the lock can never drift outside pyproject's ranges.

# Web wrapper.
